sensorboard - ESP32 sensor dashboard
====================================
sensorboard is a small sensor dashboard built with PHP, MySQL and
JavaScript. Devices send readings as JSON to ingest.php, PHP stores
them in the database, and index.html plots them live.


Requirements
------------
In order to run sensorboard you need:

    - PHP with the PDO MySQL driver (Void Linux: php, php-mysql)
    - MariaDB or MySQL
    - curl and awk (only for simulate.sh)

The page loads Chart.js from cdnjs, so the browser needs internet
access.


Setup
-----
Copy the example files:

    cp config.example.php config.php
    cp schema.example.sql schema.sql

Edit schema.sql and set a password for the database user. Edit
config.php and put the same password there, together with a long
random API key. A key can be generated with:

    php -r 'echo bin2hex(random_bytes(32)), PHP_EOL;'

Afterwards create the database, the user and the table (as the
database root user):

    mariadb -u root -p < schema.sql

config.php and schema.sql contain secrets, keep them out of Git.


Running
-------
Start the PHP built-in web server in the project directory:

    php -S localhost:8000

and open http://localhost:8000/ in a browser. The built-in server is
meant for development only.


Simulation
----------
Without hardware, simulate.sh pretends to be a sensor and posts a
random temperature every two seconds (stop it with Ctrl+C). Run it
from the project directory, in a second terminal:

    ./simulate.sh [url]

The url defaults to http://localhost:8000/ingest.php.


Interface
---------
Devices send readings with a POST request to ingest.php, with the
API key from config.php in the X-API-Key header:

    curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/ingest.php \
        -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
        -H "X-API-Key: <api_key>" \
        -d '{"device_id":"esp32-1","sensor_type":"temperature","value":23.5}'

On success the reply is 201 {"status":"ok","id":N}. A wrong key gives
401, invalid data 422.

readings.php answers GET requests with the stored readings as JSON.
It takes the optional parameters device, limit (1-500, default 50)
and after_id (only return readings newer than this id).


Files
-----
    ingest.php          stores readings sent by devices
    readings.php        returns stored readings as JSON
    index.html          dashboard page
    style.css           dashboard styles
    app.js              dashboard logic (polling, chart, table)
    config.example.php  template for config.php
    schema.example.sql  template for schema.sql
    simulate.sh         fake sensor for testing


Notes
-----
readings.php needs no API key and traffic is plain HTTP, so do not
expose the server to untrusted networks as it is.
